description:
packages/swf/src/sprite.ts, lines 496-521: the isFirst branch for shape/drawing-object display objects has no blend mode check. When a shape or drawing-object with a non-normal blendMode is placed for the FIRST time on a symbol timeline, the code falls through to:
  - morphRatio check (lines 503-504) 
  - clipDepth check (lines 505-506)
  - visible===false check (507-509)
  - hasEnabledFilters check (510-518)
  - plain encodePlaceObject2 fallback (line 520)

PlaceObject2 cannot carry blend modes; the blend mode is silently dropped.

The posChanged branch (lines 659-688) DOES handle blend mode correctly: line 667 checks hasShapeBlend and emits encodePlaceObject3WithBlendMode. But the isFirst branch was never updated.

Task 1160 (now cancelled) noted this gap. Task 1110 fixed text/bitmap but not shape.

Fix: in the isFirst shape branch (lines 496-521), add a hasShapeBlend check between the filters check and the plain fallback:
  const hasShapeBlend = displayObj.type === 'shape' && !!blendMode && blendMode !== 'normal';
  if (...filters...) { ... }
  else if (hasShapeBlend) {
    const placeBody = encodePlaceObject3WithBlendMode(charId, depth, x, y, blendMode, filters, objTransform, undefined, undefined, undefined, undefined, cacheAsBitmap);
    spriteTags.push(encodeTag(Tag.PlaceObject3, placeBody));
  } else { ... }

Also add blendMode to colorEffectKey computation for shape objects (sprite.ts ~line 440-451) so a blend mode change between keyframes correctly triggers posChanged. The same gap exists in compile.ts shape colorEffectKey but that is a separate file.
